  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward if sentiment is negative or neutral, especially after recent price spikes.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp upward moves in price (e.g., after +0.50 sentiment), as markets often correct quickly.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 7-day average, reduce by 5-10% to align with historical volatility.",
    "Increase downward bias if sentiment remains flat or negative over 3+ consecutive days, indicating potential downward pressure.",
    "Avoid over-optimism in early forecast periods (e.g., first 5 days of 30d horizon) — model tends to overestimate short-term gains.",
    "If sentiment is positive but price is trending downward, reduce forecast slope to avoid lagged overcorrection."
